  "content": {
    "_uid": "a709c1a5-68ab-55f1-6d66-fe862e0c1893",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "7359c7f5-78ef-9553-83cd-aaa822bec9ab",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The first Clinical Simulation Educators Programme Online (CSEPO) was offered in October 2020 and had 24 registered participants from Pakistan and Kenya, 19 of whom completed. Upon faculty evaluation and review, it was clear that through different teaching strategies, participants had covered core essentials of SBE and felt confident in utilizing clinical simulation as a teaching strategy. Participants also expressed their appreciation towards the course design and its delivery.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "With this positive evaluation, and the demand to provide educators with up-to-date knowledge in clinical simulation, the next offering of CSEPO is in April 2021 and has been redesigned for a more manageable 6 weeks. The course will be marketed to a more international audience, allowing participants to interact and network with colleagues from across the globe. CSEPO will not replace the existing CSEP, a faster-paced hands-on course, but will add to our repertoire of educational offerings by CIME.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
