    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Clinical Simulation Educators Programme (CSEP) has proven to be vital in developing the capacity of faculty to conduct simulation-based education (SBE) at the Aga Khan University. Offered by the centre's qualified educators, with contributions from experienced faculty, this five-day intensive in-person programme is tailored to provide just-in-time learning to participants priming them with skills and knowledge to incorporate clinical simulation in their teaching tool-box. With the advent of the pandemic and due to the high demand for the CSEP internally and internationally, the course was adapted to 8 weeks Online allowing participants to have both synchronous and asynchronous sessions. Once per week, live teaching and demonstration sessions introduced themed participant-led seminars. These written papers posed relevant questions that were taken up on the discussion forum. The student presenter then moderated the discussion and concluded the main points at the end of the week. All students had the opportunity to present a paper and have their ideas critically appraised by their colleagues. Participation dramatically improved after 2-3 weeks.",
